      ],
      "solution": "$u_5 = u_1 r^4 = 324$ ...(1) and $u_{10} = u_1 r^9 = 78\\,732$ ...(2). Now $\\frac{u_1 r^9}{u_1 r^4} = \\frac{78\\,732}{324} \\implies r^5 = 243 \\implies r = \\sqrt[5]{243} \\implies r = 3$. Using (1), $u_1(3)^4 = 324 \\implies 81u_1 = 324 \\implies u_1 = 4$. Thus $u_n = 4 \\times 3^{n-1}$.",
